        <headline>** DUAL BLEED ALERT ** - BLEED AND PRESSURISATION REVIEW</headline>
        <description>** DUAL BLEED ALERT - THIS WORK ORDER CANNOT BE PUSHED FURTHER THAN 24/11/2025.

BACKGROUND: THIS AIRCRAFT HAS TRIGGERED A DUAL BLEED ALERT, WITH BOTH LH AND RH BLEED DUCT PRESSURES BEING LOW IN DESCENT.
THIS WORK ORDER HAS BEEN RAISED TO ACTION THE LH SIDE BLEED ISSUE FIRST.

ACTION:

1) OBSERVING ALL SAFETY PRECAUTIONS, GAIN ACCESS TO THE AIRCRAFT.

2) USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08 ) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #1 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.     

 * RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM        

** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.

3) INSPECT #1 HSR FOR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM.  

4) CLOSELY INSPECT LH PRSOV FOR NOTCHY BEHAVIOUR, INABILITY TO REMAIN OPEN AND ACTUATOR BODY LEAKAGE.

5) REPLACE THE LH HSR IAW AMM 36-11-07/401 -LATEST REV.

6) RECTIFY ANY OTHER DEFECTS AND RECORD ANY ADDITIONAL FINDINGS IN THIS WORK ORDER.

7) RETURN AC TO SERVICE WITH ALL FINDINGS FROM THIS WO DOCUMENTED AND CLOSED EITHER THROUGH POSITIVE MAINTENANCE ACTION OR AN ACCEPTABLE DEFERRAL.  

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.     

**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
